#EMBEDDED_NOTES
#This example, combined with the corresponding overlaid example, demonstrates how to use two CarSim S-Function blocks in a single Simulink model to simulate an Active Cruise Control example.
#
#The trailing vehicle (this vehicle) has a radar-based active cruise control system that tracks the vehicle in front of it (overlay).
#
#In order to run this example with Simulink, follow these steps:
#
#1. If running a 32-bit version of Simulink, then proceed to Step 2.
#
#If running a 64-bit version of Simulink, an adjustment will have to be made. Click on the blue link under the "Send to Simulink" button -- Radar Active Cruise: Second Car (Ext. Sen.) -- and read the notes on that Models: Simulink screen. Change the specified DLL file name for the respective 64-bit math model DLL.
#
#After this change, return to this Run Control screen.
#
#2. Click the "Send to Simulink" button from this Run Control screen (i.e., the second vehicle)
#
#3. Click on the overlaid Run Control blue link for the first vehicle -- "Radar Active Cruise: First Car (Ext. Sen.)" -- to view that Run Control dataset, and click the "Send to Simulink" button (if you haven't done so already).
#
#4. Go to Simulink and run the model. Output data are generated for both vehicle models.
#
#For more details on this example, please see the Technical Memo: "Example: Running Multiple Vehicles in Simulink."
#END_EMBEDDED_NOTES

